Endpoint Testing (Online Predictions)

Once the model is deployed, validate that the endpoint accepts requests and returns predictions.

1. Retrieve Endpoint Details
gcloud ai endpoints describe ENDPOINT_ID \
  --region=us-central1

2. Create a Test Request Payload

Example request.json:
{
  "instances": [
    {
      "text": "Hello Vertex AI"
    }
  ]
}

3. Send a Prediction Request
gcloud ai endpoints predict ENDPOINT_ID \
  --region=us-central1 \
  --json-request=request.json

Example response:
{
  "predictions": [
    {
      "label": "positive",
      "score": 0.98
    }
  ]
}

4. Test Using REST API
Obtain an access token:
TOKEN=$(gcloud auth print-access-token)

Invoke the endpoint:
curl -X POST \
-H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
https://us-central1-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/PROJECT_ID/locations/us-central1/endpoints/ENDPOINT_ID:predict \
-d @request.json

5. Measure Latency
time gcloud ai endpoints predict ENDPOINT_ID \
  --region=us-central1 \
  --json-request=request.json

6. Negative Testing
Invalid Input
JSON
{
  "invalid": "payload"
}

Empty Input
{
  "instances": []
}

7. Check Prediction Logs
gcloud logging read \
'resource.type="aiplatform.googleapis.com/Endpoint"' \
--limit=50

SRE Validation Record

MODEL_ID        = <MODEL_ID>
ENDPOINT_ID     = <ENDPOINT_ID>

TEST_CASE_1     = Valid prediction
STATUS          = PASS

TEST_CASE_2     = Invalid payload
STATUS          = PASS

TEST_CASE_3     = Empty payload
STATUS          = PASS

AVERAGE_LATENCY = <ms>

OVERALL_STATUS  = READY FOR PRODUCTION


